From: Mobile NixOS porting work <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 14:45:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] selinux: ignore host PF_MAX when building policy tools

genheaders and mdp are host utilities. Their class map describes the target
4.14 kernel, but the compile-time guard reads PF_MAX from the host libc. Modern
libc headers therefore reject this old source even though the target address
families did not change.

Drop the host-header guard. This does not alter the target class map.
---
 security/selinux/include/classmap.h | 4 ----
 1 file changed, 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/security/selinux/include/classmap.h b/security/selinux/include/classmap.h
index 4d7e762..b9006ad 100644
--- a/security/selinux/include/classmap.h
+++ b/security/selinux/include/classmap.h
@@ -243,6 +243,2 @@ struct security_class_mapping secclass_map[] = {
 	{ NULL }
   };
-
-#if PF_MAX > 44
-#error New address family defined, please update secclass_map.
-#endif
-- 
2.51.0
